# Siemens SENTRON PAC3200 power monitoring device, Modbus TCP over the built-in Ethernet port.
# The device ships with SEAbus TCP; switch the protocol to MODBUS TCP on the display first.
# Addresses are the manual's offsets, which are the addresses sent on the wire.
# Read multi-register values from their first register only: starting a read in the middle of a value returns an error.
# Modbus RTU needs the optional PAC RS485 module; it uses the same offsets.
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Siemens
@model=SENTRON PAC3200
@vendor_website=siemens.com
@description=Panel-mount power monitoring device (7KM2111 / 7KM2112), Modbus TCP
@source=Siemens, "SENTRON PAC3200 Power Monitoring Device" manual, A5E01168664B-04 (02/2008); https://support.industry.siemens.com/cs/document/26504150
@protocol=tcp
@port=502
@unit_id=1
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@enum_connection_type=0=3P4W|1=3P3W|2=3P4WB|3=3P3WB|4=1P2W
@enum_no_yes=0=No|1=Yes

